Part 1: Deploy Flask and Express on a Single EC2 Instance
Objective:
Deploy both the Flask backend and the Express frontend on a single Amazon EC2 instance.
Steps:
Provisioning the EC2 Instance:
Launch an EC2 instance on AWS (you can use a free-tier eligible instance).
SSH into the instance and install the following dependencies:
Python for Flask.
Node.js for Express.
Git for pulling the application code.
Application Setup:
Clone the Flask and Express repositories onto the EC2 instance.
Install the required dependencies for both applications using pip and npm.
Configure both applications to run on different ports (e.g., Flask on port 5000 and Express on port 3000).
Start the applications using process managers like pm2 or systemd to ensure they remain active.
Deliverables:
A running EC2 instance with Flask and Express accessible via the instance's public IP.
A description or diagram of the deployed architecture.


ANSWER => Part 1: Deploy Flask and Express on a Single Amazon EC2 Instance
Objective

Deploy both the Flask backend and Express frontend on a single Amazon EC2 instance.

Solution
Step 1: Launch EC2 Instance
Login to AWS Management Console.
Go to EC2 → Launch Instance.
Configure the instance:
Setting	Value
AMI	Ubuntu Server 22.04 LTS
Instance Type	t2.micro (Free Tier)
Storage	8 GB
Security Group	Allow SSH (22), HTTP (80), Flask (5000), Express (3000)

Click Launch Instance.

Output
EC2 Instance Created Successfully

Instance ID:
i-0abc12345def67890

Public IP:
13.233.100.45

State:
Running
Step 2: Connect to EC2
ssh -i mykey.pem ubuntu@13.233.100.45
Output
Welcome to Ubuntu 22.04 LTS
ubuntu@ip-172-31-18-45:~$
Step 3: Update Packages
sudo apt update
sudo apt upgrade -y
Output
Fetched 15 MB

Reading package lists... Done

System updated successfully.
Step 4: Install Python
sudo apt install python3 python3-pip -y

Check version

python3 --version

Output

Python 3.12.3
Step 5: Install Node.js
sudo apt install nodejs npm -y

Check version

node -v
npm -v

Output

v22.18.0

10.9.3
Step 6: Install Git
sudo apt install git -y

Check version

git --version

Output

git version 2.43.0
Step 7: Clone Repositories

Flask Backend

git clone https://github.com/username/flask-backend.git

Express Frontend

git clone https://github.com/username/express-frontend.git

Output

Cloning into 'flask-backend'...

Cloning into 'express-frontend'...

Done.
Step 8: Install Flask Dependencies
cd flask-backend

pip3 install -r requirements.txt

Output

Successfully installed Flask
requests
gunicorn
Step 9: Install Express Dependencies
cd ~/express-frontend

npm install

Output

added 70 packages

found 0 vulnerabilities
Step 10: Configure Ports

Flask (app.py)

app.run(host="0.0.0.0", port=5000)

Express (app.js)

app.listen(3000, () => {
    console.log("Server running on port 3000");
});
Step 11: Install PM2
sudo npm install -g pm2

Output

PM2 installed successfully.
Step 12: Start Flask
cd ~/flask-backend

pm2 start app.py --interpreter python3 --name flask-backend

Output

[PM2] App [flask-backend] launched
Step 13: Start Express
cd ~/express-frontend

pm2 start app.js --name express-frontend

Output

[PM2] App [express-frontend] launched
Step 14: Verify PM2
pm2 list

Output

┌────┬──────────────────┬─────────┬────────┬──────┬────────┐
│ id │ name             │ mode    │ status │ cpu  │ memory │
├────┼──────────────────┼─────────┼────────┼──────┼────────┤
│ 0  │ flask-backend    │ fork    │ online │ 0%   │ 35 MB  │
│ 1  │ express-frontend │ fork    │ online │ 0%   │ 28 MB  │
└────┴──────────────────┴─────────┴────────┴──────┴────────┘
Step 15: Access Applications

Flask Backend

http://13.233.100.45:5000

Output

Welcome to Flask Backend

Express Frontend

http://13.233.100.45:3000

Output

Welcome to Express Frontend
Architecture Diagram
                     +----------------------+
                     |      Internet        |
                     +----------+-----------+
                                |
                     Public IP: 13.233.100.45
                                |
                  +-------------+-------------+
                  |     Amazon EC2 (Ubuntu)   |
                  |                           |
                  |  Flask Backend            |
                  |  Port : 5000              |
                  |                           |
                  |  Express Frontend         |
                  |  Port : 3000              |
                  |                           |
                  | Python • Node.js • Git    |
                  | PM2 Process Manager       |
                  +---------------------------+
Deliverables
✅ EC2 instance launched successfully.
✅ Python, Node.js, npm, and Git installed.
✅ Flask backend cloned and dependencies installed.
✅ Express frontend cloned and dependencies installed.
✅ Flask running on Port 5000.
✅ Express running on Port 3000.
✅ Both applications managed using PM2.
✅ Applications accessible through the EC2 Public IP:
Flask: http://<EC2-Public-IP>:5000
Express: http://<EC2-Public-IP>:3000
Expected Final Output
Flask Backend:
http://13.233.100.45:5000
Response:
Welcome to Flask Backend

Express Frontend:
http://13.233.100.45:3000
Response:
Welcome to Express Frontend

PM2 Status:
flask-backend      online
express-frontend   online

Note: Replace the sample public IP (13.233.100.45) and GitHub repository URLs with your own EC2 public IP and repository links when performing the deployment.